# Class: obo:FOODON_02000279 (lamb tenderloin)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_02000279 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_02000279 "A whole cut that is derived from the short loin or any loin item that includes the sirloin. Because of its anatomical location, the tenderloin is the least exercised muscle in the carcass thus the name “Tender” Loin. The cut location is from underneath the finger bones in the short loin and the hipbone in the sirloin."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_02000279 <https://www.ams.usda.gov/sites/default/files/media/Lamb_IMPS200Series_2022.pdf>)
