# Class: obo:FOODON_02000466 (beef stew meat)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:FOODON_02000466 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:FOODON_02000466 "A piece of boneless beef derived from any primal cut intended for stewing. Stew is typically uniform in shape and no more than ½-inch in diameter."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:FOODON_02000466 <https://www.meattrack.com/app/beef-cuts/#453>)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:FOODON_02000466 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5275-8866>)
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:date obo:FOODON_02000466 "2026-04-18T11:31:46Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:FOODON_02000466 "beef stew chunk"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_02000466 "The name “Stew” originates from a method of cooking where small pieces of meat are simmered in water or other liquid until its tender. Stew Meat must be free from bones, cartilages, lymph glands, and connective tissue. In dimensions, Stew is smaller than Cubes and Kabobs. Stew should be uniform in shape and no more than a ½-inch in diameter."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:FOODON_02000466 "beef stew meat"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:FOODON_02000466 obo:FOODON_02000405)

